{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788327021,"nonce":"jBb/6+uFqMh3LM4wfaWhQEPAO8Y=","title":"**This killed three colonists and ended run `m1-20260901`.** Post-mortem output A-3. There is no protocol workaround.","message":"A `ButcherSpot` was built and a bill queued the normal way:\n\n```\nbuild      {def:\"ButcherSpot\", at:\"114,138\"}            -\u003e placed\nbill-add   {bench:103250, recipe:\"ButcherCorpseFlesh\",\n            repeat:\"forever\"}                            -\u003e ok, uid Bill_ButcherCorpseFlesh_6\n```\n\nThe bill then read perfectly healthy for the rest of the run and **never produced a single meat**:\n\n```\nbills -\u003e {\"recipe\":\"ButcherCorpseFlesh\",\"suspended\":false,\n          \"ingredient_radius\":\"unlimited\",\"filter\":null,\n          \"next_ingredient_search_tick\":3606060}\n```\n\nWith a **fresh wild boar corpse (hp 95%, unforbidden) lying on the butcher spot's own cell (114,138)**, every attempt to work it was refused:\n\n```\nprioritize {pawn:91381, work:\"DoBillsButcherFlesh\", thing:103250}\n  -\u003e ok:true, rejected: [\"blocked: Missing 1x corpses\"]\n```\n\nSix corpses were on the map — 2 wild boar, 2 deer, a donkey, a human, roughly 600 meat. The colony starved to death surrounded by them.\n\n\n`filter: null` on a bill whose recipe has a `fixedIngredientFilter` means it matches nothing. Setting it appears to work and then does not stick:\n\n```\nbill-set {bench:103250, index:0, allow:[\"Corpses\"]}\n  -\u003e ok:true, changed:[{field:\"filter\", value:{\n       ops:[{op:\"allow\", kind:\"category\", def:\"Corpses\", defs_delta:39}],\n       summary:{allowed_defs:154, universe:\"recipe-fixed\"}}}]\n       note: \"Bill.ExposeData NARROWS this filter during the SAVING pass for any\n              recipe with a fixedIngredientFilter (DESIGN decisions log 2026-08-3…)\"\n\nbills (next call) -\u003e {\"recipe\":\"ButcherCorpseFlesh\", \"filter\":null}\n```\n\n39 defs added, `allowed_defs: 154`, and it reads back `null`. **The verb's own note names the mechanism** — so this is a known behaviour whose consequence has not been followed through: a bill created through the protocol is permanently inert for any recipe with a fixed ingredient filter.\n\nRemoving and re-adding the bill resets `next_ingredient_search_tick` to 0 (which is genuinely useful — see \"adjacent\" below) but does not give it a filter, so the next search fails identically.\n\n\n- **Raw corpses are not food.** `consume {pawn, thing:\u003ccorpse\u003e}` returns `cannot-eat: this pawn cannot ever eat this`. Butchering is the only route from corpse to nutrition.\n- Hunting produces *more corpses*, so a working hunter makes the problem worse, not better.\n- Nothing else in the verb surface converts a corpse.\n\nSo on any map where stored food runs out — a winter, a fire, a raid — a colony driven through this protocol **cannot eat its own kills**. That is the whole failure of this run.\n\n\n1. `bill-add` produces a bill that can actually be worked. For a recipe with a `fixedIngredientFilter`, the new bill's ingredient filter defaults to that recipe's own default (what the game's own \"add bill\" button produces), not to an empty filter. Proving it: `bill-add` a `ButcherCorpseFlesh` bill with a fresh animal corpse in reach, advance, assert `Meat_*` appears.\n2. `bill-set`'s filter edits **persist across a read**. If `Bill.ExposeData` narrowing genuinely prevents that for fixed-filter recipes, the verb must say so at write time and refuse, rather than reporting `defs_delta: 39` for a change that evaporates.\n3. `bills` distinguishes \"no filter published\" from \"filter is empty\". `filter: null` currently reads like a serialization gap and is in fact the reason the bill is dead.\n4. A bill that has failed N consecutive ingredient searches is reported as such — `production-still-runs` already says `next_ingredient_search_tick` is \"the only observable proof either way\", and this run proves the point: the field was in the future for days and the checklist has no flag for it.\n5. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-bill-filter.py` on a bench: add a butcher bill, assert it matches a corpse; `bill-set` a filter change, re-read, assert it persisted; assert a starving colony with corpses in reach actually eats.\n\n\n- **`next_ingredient_search_tick` in the FUTURE is the \"this bill is asleep\" signal.** It backs off after a failed search, so a bill that failed while its ingredients were forbidden stays dead long after they are freed. Re-creating the bill resets it to 0. That is a genuinely useful diagnostic and belongs in `production-still-runs`.\n- `prioritize` takes a **`WorkGiverDef`**, not a work type (`Cooking` is refused; `DoBillsButcherFlesh` is the name), and additionally requires `thing` or `cell` — \"the game's work-giver menu has both forms and they are different orders\". Its `blocked:` reason is the most useful diagnostic in the whole bill surface and is how this defect was finally cornered.","files":null}]}